# ==============================================================================
# VehicleSentinel: Multi-Host & Microservices Environment Configuration Template
# ==============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env and configure as needed:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# If the 5 database microservices (IIB, VAHAN, Police, ANPR, E-Challan) are hosted
# on another laptop, set REMOTE_HOST to that laptop's LAN IP (e.g. 192.168.1.50).
#
# If REMOTE_HOST is commented out, empty, or missing, the system automatically
# falls back to our own locally hosted APIs (127.0.0.1).
# ==============================================================================

# --- Security (REQUIRED; the SAME .env must be on every laptop) ---
# Do not fill these in by hand. Run once, on one laptop:
#     python -m backend.security init-env
# It writes .env with a random FEDERATION_SECRET (signs every Mediator <-> agency request)
# and AUTH_USERS (admin / police / insurer, PBKDF2 password hashes) and prints the passwords
# once. Then copy that .env to the other laptops.
# FEDERATION_SECRET=<64 hex chars>
# AUTH_USERS=admin:ADMIN:<salt$hash>,police:POLICE:<salt$hash>,insurer:INSURER:<salt$hash>
# SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=28800        # login session length
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=300        # requests per client IP per minute at the Mediator

# --- Four-laptop demo (see docs/context_discovery.md) ---
#   laptop 1: python start_system.py --services mediator,frontend   (needs the HOST_* lines below)
#   laptop 2: python start_system.py --services vahan,iib
#   laptop 3: python start_system.py --services police,echallan
#   laptop 4: python start_system.py --services anpr

# --- Global Remote Host (uncomment to point all 5 microservices to another laptop) ---
# REMOTE_HOST=192.168.1.50

# --- Or Individual Service Host Overrides (if hosted across multiple machines) ---
# HOST_IIB=192.168.1.50
# HOST_VAHAN=192.168.1.50
# HOST_POLICE=192.168.1.50
# HOST_ANPR=192.168.1.50
# HOST_ECHALLAN=192.168.1.50
# HOST_MEDIATOR=127.0.0.1
#   On the services laptop, the e-Challan service sends cache-invalidation webhooks to
#   whoever called it (normally the Mediator). Set HOST_MEDIATOR or URL_MEDIATOR there
#   only if the Mediator must be reached at a different address.

# --- Ports Configuration (Defaults to 5001-5006, 3000) ---
# PORT_FRONTEND=3000
# PORT_MEDIATOR=5001
# PORT_IIB=5002
# PORT_VAHAN=5003
# PORT_POLICE=5004
# PORT_ANPR=5005
# PORT_ECHALLAN=5006

# --- Cache Settings ---
# CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=300
